            <ArticleTitle>Elective surgery days after myocardial infarction: clinical and ethical considerations.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>363-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present an unusual case of verified myocardial infarction without surgery. Successful elective lumbar spine surgery was performed 4 days post-myocardial infarction during perioperative beta-blockade, after cardiology evaluation recommended surgery without further evaluation. Clinical and ethical considerations are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
